    "body": "Problem:\r\n`Completor:accept()` hands the item's range straight to `nvim_buf_set_text()`. That range is resolved when the response arrives, so text deleted before accepting (backspacing within the 200 ms debounce) leaves the range end past what is left of the line, and the accept aborts with `Invalid 'end_col': out of range`.\r\n\r\n18d6436 fixed the same staleness in `Completor:show()`, which drops an item once its range *start* falls outside the buffer. That guard does not cover the range end, and `accept()` was never given one, so this is a hole left by that fix rather than a regression of it.\r\n\r\nSolution:\r\nClamp the end of the range to the end of the line before writing. The start needs no clamp: `show()` dropped the item one event loop tick earlier if it had gone out of range.\r\n\r\nRef #35971\r\n\r\nAI-ssisted\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-08-24T12:41:58Z",
